### Point only to your new backend; provide your own API credentials in the HTTP client.
@base = http://127.0.0.1:18085/api/namespaces/lab/flows

### Structural schema
GET {{base}}/editor/schema

### No-code sends JSON as the same source text; YAML source works in the same field.
POST {{base}}/hello-editor/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{"source":"{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"namespace\":\"lab\",\"id\":\"hello-editor\",\"inputs\":{\"name\":{\"type\":\"STRING\",\"required\":true}},\"tasks\":[{\"id\":\"hello\",\"type\":\"core.Log\",\"message\":\"Hello {{ inputs.name }}\"}]}"}

### Resolve actual inputs without saving or executing
POST {{base}}/hello-editor/preview
Content-Type: application/json

{"source":"schemaVersion: 1\nnamespace: lab\nid: hello-editor\ninputs:\n  name: {type: STRING, required: true}\ntasks:\n  - {id: hello, type: core.Log, message: 'Hello {{ inputs.name }}'}","inputs":{"name":"Ada"}}

### Explicit import; 0 creates, an existing Flow requires its latest revision.
POST {{base}}/import
Content-Type: application/json

{"flows":[{"expectedRevision":0,"source":"schemaVersion: 1\nnamespace: lab\nid: hello-editor\nlabels: {team: example}\ntasks:\n  - {id: hello, type: core.Log, message: 'Hello'}"}]}

### Preserves source; add format=json or format=yaml for normalized definition
GET {{base}}/hello-editor/export?revision=1

### Only latest USER flows, not edge-policy flows
GET {{base}}?q=hello&labelKey=team&labelValue=example&limit=20&offset=0
